    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1624, 280.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_chunks_to_symbols_xx_0
  id: digital_chunks_to_symbols_xx
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: ''
    dimension: '1'
    in_type: byte
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    num_ports: '1'
    out_type: complex
    symbol_table: tx_const.points()
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [944, 256.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_constellation_decoder_cb_0
  id: digital_constellation_decoder_cb
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: Slices straight back to the 2-bit symbol value - no separate differential-decode
      step needed
    constellation: decode_const
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [576, 480.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_correlate_access_code_tag_xx_0
  id: digital_correlate_access_code_tag_xx
  parameters:
    access_code: '''''.join(format(b, ''08b'') for b in (b''\x55''*4 + b''\x1A\xCF\xFC\x1D''))'
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: Tags the bit immediately following a match against the last 4 bytes of
      the preamble + the OpenWave sync word 0x1ACFFC1D (GNU Radio's correlator caps
      access codes at 64 bits, so the full 96-bit preamble+syncword can't be used
      directly as the correlation target, though the full 8-byte preamble is still
      transmitted). This is what tells the RX side exactly which bit is the start
      of the payload, instead of guessing a bit-to-byte phase.
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    tagname: '"sync"'
    threshold: '4'
    type: byte
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [944, 592.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_diff_encoder_bb_0
  id: digital_diff_encoder_bb
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    coding: digital.DIFF_DIFFERENTIAL
    comment: Mod-8 phase accumulator. Accumulating an odd value mod 8 always flips
      the result's parity, so the transmitted point alternates between the "even"
      and "odd" halves of the ring every symbol - this is what actually makes it pi/4-QPSK
      instead of plain QPSK.
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    modulus: '8'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [648, 288.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_diff_phasor_cc_0
  id: digital_diff_phasor_cc
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: Differential phase detection - recovers the original odd-ring increment
      directly from the phase difference between consecutive symbols. Immune to constant
      carrier phase offset, so no Costas loop is needed here the way plain QPSK needs
      one.
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [400, 536.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_map_bb_0
  id: digital_map_bb
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: Symbol value (0..3) -> odd ring position (1,3,5,7). The even positions
      are never used directly as input.
    map: '[1, 3, 5, 7]'
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [480, 240.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: digital_symbol_sync_xx_0
  id: digital_symbol_sync_xx
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: RRC matched filter, alpha=0.35, done as a polyphase matched filter inside
      Symbol Sync itself rather than as a separate FIR block ahead of it. A separate
      pre-filter changes the pulse shape feeding the M&M timing error detector in
      a way that isn't accounted for by the loop's tuning, and was observed to cause
      a deterministic symbol-count offset (a "slip") during acquisition. Doing the
      matched filtering and timing recovery together in one block keeps the TED's
      operating point consistent.
    constellation: tx_const
    damping: '1.0'
    loop_bw: '0.045'
    max_dev: '1.5'
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    nfilters: nfilters
    osps: '1'
    pfb_mf_taps: firdes.root_raised_cosine(nfilters, sps*nfilters, 1.0, 0.35, 11*sps*nfilters)
    resamp_type: digital.IR_PFB_MF
    sps: sps
    ted_gain: '1.0'
    ted_type: digital.TED_MOD_MUELLER_AND_MULLER
    type: cc
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [48, 452.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
- name: filter_interp_fir_filter_xxx_0
  id: interp_fir_filter_xxx
  parameters:
    affinity: ''
    alias: ''
    comment: RRC pulse shaping, alpha=0.35
    interp: sps
    maxoutbuf: '0'
    minoutbuf: '0'
    samp_delay: '0'
    taps: firdes.root_raised_cosine(sps, sps, 1.0, 0.35, 11*sps)
    type: ccf
  states:
    bus_sink: false
    bus_source: false
    bus_structure: null
    coordinate: [1168, 328.0]
    rotation: 0
    state: enabled
